parameters.text:
=Add contextually relevant internal links to the following Taskwise blog article, using only the candidate URLs listed below. Follow every rule in the system message. If the candidate pool does not contain strong matches, add fewer links or none — do not force links.

## ARTICLE TO INTERLINK

Slug: {{ $json.slug }}

Title: {{ $json.title }}

Category: {{ $json.category }}

Tags: {{ $json.tags }}

Short summary: {{ $json.shortsummary }}

Full HTML content:
{{ $json.content }}

## CANDIDATE INTERNAL URLS

Each candidate below includes the destination URL, the page type, the title or purpose, a short description, and topical tags. Use these to judge relevance. Do not link to any URL outside this list.

{{ $json.candidate_urls }}

Expected candidate format (for reference):
[
  {
    "url": "https://www.taskwise.ai/blog/[slug]",
    "type": "blog | service | industry | landing | contact",
    "title": "Page title",
    "summary": "1-2 sentence description of what the page covers",
    "tags": "comma-separated topical tags",
    "primary_keyword": "main keyword or topic the page targets"
  }
]

## YOUR TASK

1. Read the article carefully and identify the paragraphs where a reader would benefit from a linked next step.
2. Match those paragraphs against the candidate list using the relevance standard in the system message.
3. Select anchor phrases that already exist inside the article's sentences — do not invent new sentences or add words to the article.
4. Insert <a href="..."> tags directly into the HTML, respecting the placement caps (max 2 in intro, plus body, plus optional conclusion).
5. Return the full updated article and a structured record of every link you added.

Return only the JSON object specified in the system message.
